{'review': '{\n  "review": "<<<ARTIFACT review_report>>>\\n{\\n  \\"overall_status\\": \\"NEEDS_FIXES\\",\\n  \\"quality_score\\": 6.5,\\n  \\"summary\\": {\\n    \\"critical\\": 1,\\n    \\"high\\": 2,\\n    \\"medium\\": 2,\\n    \\"low\\": 1,\\n    \\"passed_checks\\": [\\"Parameterized queries via EF Core\\", \\"Proper disposal of DbContext\\", \\"Authorization enforced on group\\", \\"UTC timestamps used\\"]\\n  },\\n  \\"findings\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-001\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"critical\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"security\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"Missing user ownership authorization (IDOR vulnerability)\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [18, 45],\\n      \\"description\\": "All endpoints fail to verify that the authenticated user owns the todo resource being accessed. Any authenticated user can read, update, or delete any todo by guessing its GUID ID.",\\n      "impact": "Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) allowing unauthorized access to other users\' todos, leading to data breach and tampering.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Add user ownership validation by extracting user ID from claims and filtering todos by UserId property. Requires Todo entity to have UserId field.",\\n      "code_before": "var todo = await dbContext.Todos.FindAsync(id);\\n\\n            return todo is null\\n                ? TypedResults.NotFound()\\n                : TypedResults.Ok(new TodoResponse(todo.Id, todo.Title, todo.Description, todo.Completed, todo.CreatedAt, todo.UpdatedAt));",\\n      "code_after": "var userId = User.FindFirst(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;\\n            if (userId == null)\\n                return TypedResults.Unauthorized();\\n\\n            var todo = await dbContext.Todos.FirstOrDefaultAsync(t => t.Id == id && t.UserId == userId);\\n\\n            return todo is null\\n                ? TypedResults.NotFound()\\n                : TypedResults.Ok(new TodoResponse(todo.Id, todo.Title, todo.Description, todo.Completed, todo.CreatedAt, todo.UpdatedAt));",\\n      "references": ["OWASP A01:2021 - Broken Access Control", "CWE-639: Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-002\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"high\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": "Missing input validation on request DTOs",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\\n      "line_range": [48, 75],\\n      "description": "CreateTodoRequest and UpdateTodoRequest parameters are used without validation. Empty/malicious titles or excessively long descriptions could cause storage issues or XSS if rendered in frontend.",\\n      "impact": "Potential storage of invalid data, denial of service via large payloads, and cross-site scripting if todo content is rendered without encoding.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Add validation attributes to DTO classes (e.g., [Required], [StringLength]) and validate model state in endpoints. Return 400 for invalid requests.",\\n      "code_before": "todosApi.MapPost(\\"/\\", async (CreateTodoRequest request, IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext> dbContextFactory) =>\\n        {\\n            using var dbContext = dbContextFactory.CreateDbContext();\\n            var now = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow;\\n            var todo = new Todo\\n            {\\n                Title = request.Title,\\n                Description = request.Description,\\n                Completed = request.Completed,\\n                CreatedAt = now,\\n                UpdatedAt = now\\n            };",\\n      "code_after": "todosApi.MapPost(\\"/\\", async (HttpContext httpContext, CreateTodoRequest request, IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext> dbContextFactory) =>\\n        {\\n            if (!httpContext.TryValidateModel(request))\\n                return TypedResults.ValidationProblem(httpContext.ModelState);\\n            \\n            using var dbContext = dbContextFactory.CreateDbContext();\\n            var now = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow;\\n            var todo = new Todo\\n            {\\n                Title = request.Title,\\n                Description = request.Description,\\n                Completed = request.Completed,\\n                CreatedAt = now,\\n                UpdatedAt = now\\n            };",\\n      "references": ["OWASP A03:2021 - Injection", "CWE-20: Improper Input Validation"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-003\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"high\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"performance\\",\\n      "title": "Missing pagination and filtering options on GET all todos",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\\n      "line_range": [18, 45],\\n      "description": "The GET /api/v1/todos endpoint returns all todos without pagination, sorting, or filtering options. With large datasets, this causes excessive memory usage, network transfer, and slow response times.",\\n      "impact": "Scalability issues: O(n) memory and bandwidth consumption, potential timeouts, and poor user experience with large todo lists.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Add query parameters for page, pageSize, sortBy, sortOrder, and filter options. Implement server-side paging with Skip/Take and return total count.",\\n      "code_before": "var todos = await query\\n                .OrderBy(t => t.CreatedAt)\\n                .Select(t => new TodoResponse(t.Id, t.Title, t.Description, t.Completed, t.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt))\\n                .ToListAsync();",\\n      "code_after": "var todos = await query\\n                .ApplySorting(sortBy, sortOrder) // Extension method\\n                .ApplyFiltering(completed) // Extension method\\n                .Skip((page - 1) * pageSize)\\n                .Take(pageSize)\\n                .Select(t => new TodoResponse(t.Id, t.Title, t.Description, t.Completed, t.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt))\\n                .ToListAsync();\\n\\n            return TypedResults.Ok(new PagedResponse<TodoResponse>\\n            {\\n                Items = todos,\\n                TotalCount = await query.CountAsync(),\\n                Page = page,\\n                PageSize = pageSize\\n            });",\\n      "references": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      "finding_id\\": \\"F-004\\",\\n      "severity": "medium",\\n      "category": "quality",\\n      "title": "Missing exception handling for database operations",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\\n      "line_range": [18, 100],\\n      "description": "Database operations (FindAsync, SaveChangesAsync) are not wrapped in try-catch blocks. Unhandled exceptions will propagate as 500 errors without logging or user-friendly messages.",\\n      "impact": "Operational blind spots: errors aren\'t logged for diagnosis, and users receive generic 500 errors instead of meaningful feedback (e.g., conflict, constraint violations).",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Wrap database operations in try-catch blocks. Log exceptions and return appropriate status codes (e.g., 409 for conflicts, 503 for transient failures).",\\n      "code_before": "await dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();\\n\\n            var todoResponse = new TodoResponse(todo.Id, todo.Title, todo.Description, todo.Completed, todo.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt);\\n            return TypedResults.CreatedAtRoute(todoResponse, \\"GetTodoById\\", new { id = todo.Id });",\\n      "code_after": "try\\n            {\\n                await dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();\\n            }\\n            catch (DbUpdateException ex) when (ex.InnerException is SqlException sqlEx && sqlEx.Number == 2601)\\n            {\\n                logger.Error(ex, \\"Duplicate key error\\");\\n                return TypedResults.Conflict(\\"A todo with this identifier already exists\\");\\n            }\\n            catch (Exception ex)\\n            {\\n                logger.Error(ex, \\"Database error\\");\\n                return TypedResults.StatusCode(503);\\n            }\\n\\n            var todoResponse = new TodoResponse(todo.Id, todo.Title, todo.Description, todo.Completed, todo.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt);\\n            return TypedResults.CreatedAtRoute(todoResponse, \\"GetTodoById\\", new { id = todo.Id });",\\n      "references": ["OWASP A09:2021 - Security Logging and Monitoring Failures"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      "finding_id\\": \\"F-005\\",\\n      "severity": "medium",\\n      "category": "quality",\\n      "title": "Inconsistent null-coalescing usage in update endpoint",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\\n      "line_range": [78, 95],\\n      "description": "The update endpoint uses null-coalescing for Title and Description but not for Completed property. This creates inconsistency where null Completed values ignore client input while other fields respect it.",\\n      "impact": "Clients cannot explicitly set Completed to false via null payload (if using nullable bool), causing confusion in API behavior.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Apply consistent null-coalescing pattern to all nullable properties or use explicit null checks. Consider making Completed non-nullable in request model if always required.",\\n      "code_before": "todo.Title = request.Title ?? todo.Title;\\n            todo.Description = request.Description ?? todo.Description;\\n            todo.Completed = request.Completed ?? todo.Completed;",\\n      "code_after": "todo.Title = request.Title ?? todo.Title;\\n            todo.Description = request.Description ?? todo.Description;\\n            todo.Completed = request.Completed.HasValue ? request.Completed.Value : todo.Completed;",\\n      "references": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      "finding_id\\": \\"F-006\\",\\n      "severity": "low",\\n      "category": "quality",\\n      "title": "Missing AsNoTracking for read-only queries",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\\n      "line_range": [18, 45],\\n      "description": "GET endpoints use tracking queries unnecessarily. Since no modifications are made to the retrieved entities, AsNoTracking() would improve performance by reducing memory overhead.",\\n      "impact": "Slightly increased memory allocation and CPU usage for read operations, impacting scalability under load.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Add AsNoTracking() to all read-only queries (GET endpoints) where entities are not modified.",\\n      "code_before": "var query = dbContext.Todos.AsQueryable();\\n\\n            if (completed.HasValue)\\n            {\\n                query = query.Where(t => t.Completed == completed.Value);\\n            }\\n\\n            var todos = await query\\n                .OrderBy(t => t.CreatedAt)\\n                .Select(t => new TodoResponse(t.Id, t.Title, t.Description, t.Completed, t.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt))\\n                .ToListAsync();",\\n      "code_after": "var query = dbContext.Todos.AsNoTracking().AsQueryable();\\n\\n            if (completed.HasValue)\\n            {\\n                query = query.Where(t => t.Completed == completed.Value);\\n            }\\n\\n            var todos = await query\\n                .OrderBy(t => t.CreatedAt)\\n                .Select(t => new TodoResponse(t.Id, t.Title, t.Description, t.Completed, t.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt))\\n                .ToListAsync();",\\n      "references": []\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"positive_observations\\": [\\n    \\"Authorization correctly applied at group level\\",\\n    \\"Proper use of DbContextFactory for scoped instances\\",\\n    \\"Consistent use of UTC timestamps\\",\\n    \\"Appropriate HTTP status codes (200, 201, 404, 204)\\",\\n    \\"GUID route constraints prevent invalid ID formats\\",\\n    \\"DTO pattern separates API contracts from entities\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n<<<ENDARTIFACT>>>"\r\n}'}